When running from vscode, all arguments in this file will be passed to the compiler.
Any line starting with "-" counts as an argument for both running and building.
Any line starting with "+" counts as a build-only argument; the "+" is replaced with "-" when passed to the compiler.
This means to disable or enable any flag, remove or add the prefix at the start of the line.

Following are the default enabled arguments:

-runcompiletimefunctions
-injectobjects
-stacktraces

Optimization arguments (enabled for builds, skipped for runs):

+inline
+opt
+localOptimizations

Optional Lua output (add "-" to enable; Grill sets the project's script mode during generation):

lua

For a list of all arguments visit the manual or run wurstscript.jar without arguments.
